Discover ING Hubs Romania
ING Hubs Romania offers 130 services in software development, data management, non-financial risk & compliance, audit, and retail operations to 24 ING units worldwide, with the help ofover 2000 high-performing engineers, risk, and operations professionals.
We started out in 2015 as ING’s software development hub, then steadily expanded our range to include more services and competencies. Now we provide borderless services with bank-wide capabilities andoperate from two locations: Bucharest and Cluj-Napoca.
Our tech capabilities remain the core of our business, with more than 1800 colleagues active in Data and Analytics Tech, Tech Foundation and Channels, Retail Core Banking and Architecture, and Global Products and Technology Services.
We enjoy a flexible way of working and a highly collaborative environment, where fair and constructive feedback is encouraged.
For us, impact isn't a perk. It's the driver of our work. We are guided and rewarded by a shared desire to make the world a better place, one innovative solution at a time. Our colleagues make it their job to do impactful things and they love doing it in good company. Do you?
TheAPI SDKis ING's core framework for developing secure, resilient, and high-performance APIs. This role offers the opportunity to work on foundational platforms that power ING's digital banking capabilities across our global technology ecosystem.
API SDK is a Spring Boot-based framework that serves as the foundation for developing APIs. It's a lightweight layer on top of Spring Boot that configures beans and filters specific to the ING landscape, including:
Service registry integration for automatic service registration and discovery
Pre-configured resilient HTTP client for inter-service communication
Security components (token validation, access control, and authorization)
Centralized logging and metrics integration with monitoring platforms
Service mesh connectivity and proxy support for polyglot architectures
Framework Development & Maintenance
Design, develop, and maintain core components of the API SDK;
Implement new features that enhance security, resilience, and observability;
Ensure backward compatibility while evolving the framework architecture;
Create and maintain the Toolkit components that underpin the framework.
Integrate with ING's infrastructure platforms (container platforms, messaging systems, API gateways);
Implement connectivity modules;
Ensure seamless integration with service mesh and service discovery;
Support both direct framework usage and proxy-based deployments.
Build intuitive APIs and configuration interfaces for framework consumers;
Create comprehensive documentation, cookbooks, and how-to guides;
Develop testing toolkits and frameworks for local development and validation;
Provide reference implementations demonstrating best practices.
Support development teams using the API SDK through internal support channels;
Review and merge community pull requests.
Technologies You'll Work With Daily
Languages & Frameworks: Java 17+, Spring Boot, Jersey, Scala, Maven, Gradle;
Infrastructure & Platforms: Kubernetes, Docker, Azure Container Registry, Azure DevOps (repos, pipelines, artifacts);
Integration & Communication: Apache Kafka and enterprise messaging systems, RESTful APIs, Service registry and discovery systems;
Observability Stack: Prometheus + Grafana, OpenTelemetry and distributed tracing, Enterprise logging and metrics platforms, ;Centralized logging infrastructure
Security: PKI infrastructure, token-based authentication, mTLS, certificate management, API Gateway technologies.
